CORE
definition.c caller.c
--dfcc main --replace-call-with-contract f
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[f\.precondition\.2\] line 1 Check requires clause of contract contract::f for function f: FAILURE$
^\[main\.precondition_instance\.1\] line 6 static array parameter .* must provide access to its declared minimum: FAILURE$
^\*\* 2 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
With DFCC, the refreshed requires clause of the contract checks the larger
linked minimum, and the call-site precondition of the replacement wrapper
checks the same linked minimum.
